<speak>My natural method is usually to remember roughly where I was sitting when I opened something. That is not a very reliable filing system, I admit. I remember an envelope being near the window, or a document being beside the newspaper, but then somebody tidies the room. I should not blame the person who tidied it; they are doing the sensible thing. The two-folder arrangement might help. One for things I still need to look at, one for things I have dealt with. If I can keep those separate, at least I will stop reopening the same letter and wondering whether I missed something.</speak>